      <div type="clause" n="35.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ECfRetr">ECf retr</ref> 35.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="ECf retr 35.2"><pb n="666" ed="#liebermann"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.1"/><hi rend="bold">Quomodo sanctus rex Edwardus propter iniquitatem et nequitiam gentis sue et maxime propter</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.2"/> <hi rend="bold">insolentiam et superbiam filiorum comitis</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.3"/> <hi rend="bold">Godwini Willelmum ducem heredem regni fecit, eo</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.4"/> <hi rend="bold">quod de Edgaro facere nequiuit.</hi> Rex autem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.5"/> Eadwardus, <hi rend="bold">ut</hi> cognouit gentis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.6"/> sue nequitiam et <hi rend="bold">precipue superbiam</hi> filiorum Godwini, scilicet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.3"/> Haroldi, <hi rend="bold">qui postea</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.7"/> <hi rend="bold">regnum inuasit</hi>†, Tosti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.8"/>, Gurti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.9"/>, Lefwini<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.10"/> <hi rend="bold">et aliorum</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.fn.a"/> <hi rend="bold">fratrum suorum,</hi> comperit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.3"/> non posse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.11"/> <hi rend="bold">fore</hi> stabile uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.12"/> <hi rend="bold">ratum quod proposuerat</hi> de Eadgaro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.13"/>, adoptauit Willelmum ducem Normannorum <hi rend="bold">in regnum, Willelmum dico nothum, id est bastardum,</hi> filium Roberti, auunculi sui, <hi rend="bold">uidelicet</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.14"/> <hi rend="bold">fratris</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.fn.d"/> <hi rend="bold">matris sue, uirum strenuum et</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.15"/> <hi rend="bold">bellicosum et fortem.</hi> Qui† postea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.16"/>, <hi rend="bold">annuente</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.17"/> Deo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.18"/>, <hi rend="spaced">debellans</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.19"/> supradictum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.20"/> Haroldum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.21"/> <hi rend="bold">Godwini filium, regnum Anglorum uictoriose adeptus est. Hec</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.22"/> <hi rend="bold">hactenus</hi><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.23"/><hi rend="bold">.</hi></ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="666"><label>printed alongside</label> <ref target="clause:ECf_35-2">ECf 35.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 666 (November 2026): read from the page images and checked against the scan’s own text layer, differences settled against the page; the words in bold are the Retractator’s changes to ECf, as Liebermann prints them.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann prints daggers after “regnum inuasit” and after “Qui”; in the outer margin of the ECf retr column, beside “regnum inuasit†”, he gives the date †1066.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.fn.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. Will. Malmesbur.</hi> II 228: Rex Edwardus, quod Godwini uideret inualescere filios, . . Willelmo successionem Angliae dedit; erat ille consanguineus, filius Roberti; <hi rend="italic">vielleicht Quelle für ECf. oder aus derselben Vorlage; doch sagte Eadward Wilhelmen die Thronfolge <hi rend="spaced">vor</hi></hi> 1057 <hi rend="italic">zu; Verf. irrt also in der Begründung.</hi> Harold II. <hi rend="italic">nennt er gemäss Normannischem Kanzleibrauche nicht</hi> rex. <hi rend="italic">Dessen drei Brüder stehen auch</hi> Ann. Anglosax. 1066; <hi rend="italic">die Zufügung des Retr. irrt, da Swen todt, Wulfnoth Geisel bei Wilhelm I. war</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Will. Malmesbur. II 228: Rex Edwardus, quod Godwini uideret inualescere filios, . . Willelmo successionem Angliae dedit; erat ille consanguineus, filius Roberti; perhaps the source of ECf, or from the same exemplar; but Edward promised William the succession before 1057, so the author errs in the reason he gives. In keeping with Norman chancery usage he does not call Harold II rex. Harold’s three brothers also appear in the Ann. Anglosax. 1066; the Retr.’s addition is wrong, since Swein was dead and Wulfnoth a hostage with William I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.fn.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. Matth.</hi> 22, 18</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Matth. 22, 18</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.fn.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vielmehr Vetters; s. o.</hi> 34, 2<hi rend="italic">e</hi><hi rend="superscript">e</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rather of his cousin; see above, 34, 2e, note e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.fn.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vielmehr Brudersohnes</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rather of the brother’s son</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lb Hv;</hi> Edwardus adoptauit in regem W. ducem <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> Item de bono rege Edwardo <hi rend="italic">Lond; theilweise vor</hi> 35<hi rend="superscript">14</hi> <hi rend="italic">Pl S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so Lb Hv; Edwardus adoptauit in regem W. ducem Cb; Item de bono rege Edwardo Lond; partly before 35, note 14, Pl S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">per <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">per Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uero <hi rend="italic">Hv Ph</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uero Hv Ph</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ne. ge. su. <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ne. ge. su. Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">post eum <hi rend="italic">Lb Va Ph;</hi> poste <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">post eum Lb Va Ph; poste K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Esti <hi rend="italic">Hv;</hi> Thosti <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Esti Hv; Thosti Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gurthi <hi rend="italic">Cb Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Gurthi Cb Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Lesw. <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Lesw. Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fore esse sta. <hi rend="italic">Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fore esse sta. Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ad <hi rend="italic">Va; fehlt Hv, wo</hi> ratus</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ad Va; lacking in Hv, where ratus</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Aedelinge (Eadeling <hi rend="italic">K</hi>) <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Lond adds Aedelinge (Eadeling K)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. f. m. s. <hi rend="italic">aus Cb Lb Lond; fehlt übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. f. m. s. from Cb Lb Lond; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Va Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Va Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">post <hi rend="italic">Va</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">post Va</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D. a. <hi rend="italic">Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">D. a. Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Domino <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Domino Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ando <hi rend="italic">Cb Hv Lond; fehlt Co;</hi> -lante <hi rend="italic">Lb;</hi> -auit <hi rend="italic">Ph</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ando Cb Hv Lond; lacking in Co; -lante Lb; -auit Ph</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H. s. <hi rend="italic">Va;</hi> H. predic. <hi rend="italic">Ph</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H. s. Va; H. predic. Ph</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Herald. <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> supradictum <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Herald. Cb; Lb adds supradictum</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H. h. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hv</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H. h. lacking in Hv</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECfRetr_35-2.lnote.la.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">666</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> Genealogia Norman. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Genealogia Norman. follows in Lond</seg></note>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude-crib" ana="#fromLatin">How the holy King Edward, because of the iniquity and wickedness of his people and especially because of the insolence and pride of the sons of Earl Godwine, made Duke William heir of the kingdom, because he could not do so with Edgar. But King Edward, when he knew the wickedness of his people and especially the pride of the sons of Godwine, namely of Harold, who afterwards invaded the kingdom†, Tostig, Gyrth, Leofwine and their other brothers, found that what he had proposed concerning Edgar could not be stable or ratified, [and] adopted William, duke of the Normans, into the kingdom, William, I say, <hi rend="italic">nothus</hi>, that is, the bastard, son of Robert, his uncle, namely his mother's brother, a vigorous and warlike and brave man. Who† afterwards, with God's assent, defeating the aforesaid Harold, son of Godwine, victoriously obtained the kingdom of the English. So much for this.</ab>
      </div>
